description:
Write `json(v)` that turns Lua values into JSON text with no spaces:

- `nil` is `null`, booleans `true`/`false`;
- integers with `tostring`; floats with `string.format("%.14g", x)`; NaN and infinities raise an error;
- strings in double quotes, with `"` `\` and the control characters escaped: `\n`, `\r`, `\t` by name, others as `\u00XX` (lower-case hex);
- a non-empty table whose keys are exactly 1 to n is an array `[...]`; any other non-empty table is an object `{...}` with its keys sorted, and every key must be a string (otherwise an error); the empty table is `[]`;
- `json(v, true)` instead writes the empty table as `{}`.

starter.solution.lua:
function json(v, empty_as_object)
    return tostring(v)
end
